# User Environment (example)

Copy this file to `USER.md` in the same directory and replace it with your own
machine setup. `USER.md` is gitignored; this `.example` is the shared template
that ships in the repo.

## Environment

Your dev machine(s) and how they connect — so an agent doesn't assume one
layout. For example:

> Two dev machines over SSH: `<user>@<laptop>` (macOS, workspace at `~/workspace/`)
> and `<user>@<desktop>` (Linux, workspace at `~/code/`). Note any per-machine
> path differences.

## Reference Library

Where your shared external references live, e.g. `~/<workspace>/reference/`.
Start a session from `reference/project/<project>.md`; avoid heavy project-local
`reference/` dirs.
